Why MIT, and what it means for this particular tool:

* MIT was chosen over a copyleft licence so that ROM packagers, mirror
  operators and downstream maintainers can redistribute a fixed build. That is
  the point: the fixes to the write path and the recovery path are only useful
  if people are legally allowed to ship them.
* The disclaimer above is not boilerplate here. This software runs as root and
  rewrites a Wi-Fi calibration file on your device. It is provided with no
  warranty of any kind, and you accept that risk by using it. Read README.md
  ("Safety, backups and recovery") before you install it.
* The licence covers the source in this repository only. It does not grant any
  right to use this software against a device you do not own or a network you
  are not authorized to use; see "Intended use and authorization" in README.md.
* No copyright holder or contact address is recorded anywhere in this
  repository (verified: no `git remote`, no author metadata in any tracked
  file). "MacChanger contributors" is therefore used as the copyright holder.
  Whoever maintains this distribution should replace it with a real identity.
